# What the service image build must not carry.
#
# The build context is the whole repository, and everything below is either a
# build output, a working directory, or somebody's local state. The first build
# of this image sent 103.9 GB to the daemon, because a working tree holds a
# root `target`, one `target` for each crate a test ran in, a `data` directory,
# and a soak `run` directory. Every pattern here is `**`-prefixed where the
# thing appears at more than one depth: a bare `target` matches the root one
# and nothing else.

**/target
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache

data
run
.git
.deps
# ...except the transport the dashboard imports by relative path. It is a
# checkout of a pinned release, not somebody's local state.
!.deps/csilgen/transports/typescript
tallyowl.local.yaml
*.local.env
